  "notes": [
    "Source: NeurIPS 2024 proceedings PDF (38th Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems), 30 pages: main text (pages 1-10), references (10-14), appendix A.1-A.8 (15-25) and the NeurIPS Paper Checklist (24-30). Authors: Chaoyi Pan, Zeji Yi, Guanya Shi, Guannan Qu. Converted from the user's copy of the PDF after reader highlights were removed (text unchanged). External metadata: arXiv:2407.01573.",
    "Mathematics is transcribed to LaTeX, taken from the authors' arXiv v1 TeX source where it matches and checked against the PDF; the PDF wins where they differ. Camera-ready-only material transcribed from the PDF: the Langevin-MCMC paragraph of Section 2, several sentences on pages 8-10, the Acknowledgments, the bibliography, the notation table A.1, Appendix A.6-A.8, Algorithm 3, Table 7, Figures 7-9 and the checklist.",
    "Equation (1d) on PDF page 3 is printed as 'T - 1.3'; the trailing 3 is a stray character in the camera-ready (arXiv source: 'T-1.'). It is reproduced as printed. Headings A.7 and A.8 are printed 'Abalation', A.4 'Explaination'.",
    "Footnote markers in the text are written [^n]; the footnote text is the item starting 'Footnote n:' on the same page. Algorithms 1-3 are kept as images, each followed by a line-by-line transcription.",
    "Appendix floats were moved back into their own sections with a reading order (Algorithm 3 and Figure 7 into A.6, Figure 8 into A.7, Figure 9 into A.8), and Footnote 1 follows the paragraph after equations (1a)-(1d); other floats sit at paragraph boundaries near their printed position, which can be in the neighbouring subsection (Algorithm 2 in 4.3, Figure 4 in 5.1, Tables 5-6 after A.5.4). Table 2 prints the MBD column in bold; the CSV does not carry bold.",
    "Table cells with mathematics hold LaTeX strings in the CSV (Table 1, the notation table table-a1-notation, the Table 4 header, the Table 6 learning rates). In the inline Markdown copies of these tables the builder escapes every backslash, so a cell reads '$\\\\lambda$' there: read it as '$\\lambda$'; the CSV files hold the single-backslash strings. Coloured words and symbols in captions (red 'MBD', blue 'Gaussian Process-based Bayesian Optimization', green 'data augmentation', the green star and circle of Figure 6) are reproduced without colour; the symbols are written as ★ and ●. Underlined initials of 'Model-Based Diffusion' in the abstract are not represented. Bar heights of Figures 7-9 exist only in the images.",
    "Statement italics are not kept: Definitions 1 and 3 and Propositions 2, 4 and 5 are printed in italics, and the roman text that follows a statement (for example the remark after Proposition 2 beginning 'The condition on the polynomial bounds') is commentary, not part of the statement. References [16] and [21] print raw '$\\mathbb{R}^n $' / '$\\mathbb{R}^d $' and reference [36] prints 'Large-Scale -Regularized' with the l1 symbol missing; these are reproduced as printed."
  ],
